id: pm-fr4dg8
title: "Release ratchet verdicts are a property of the working copy, not the commit: gitignored installs and clone-local git config decide three populations, so an identical commit passes locally and fails in CI"
description: ""
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,determinism,gate,parity,release
created_at: "2026-08-05T17:56:58.978Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-12T22:36:36.376Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-05T18:11:14.193Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-05T18:11:14.193Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The gate materializes a commit view containing exactly the files the next commit would carry (git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard) and measures there; a --working-copy escape hatch and an explicit --pm-path both bypass it; A fresh clone of the same commit and a maintainer working copy produce byte-identical observed populations for every declared selector; The receipt names the measurement scope so a reader can tell which tree produced the verdict; Unit coverage exercises commit-view materialization, the hardlink-to-copy fallback, the pending-deletion path, and the working-copy bypass"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Added materializeCommitView and contextForCommitView to the gate, routed the default measurement pass through the view, kept --working-copy and an explicit --pm-path as bypasses, and re-baselined the one honestly mis-measured declaration from 195 to 204 with the reason recorded in the declaration note."
expected_result: The same commit yields the same ratchet verdict on every machine.
actual_result: "It now does: the gate first reproduced the hosted failure locally for the first time, then passed identically in commit-view and working-copy modes."
